From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Praschl <praschlpaul@g-p.at>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 17:16:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 060/117] spi: apple: derive T8010 DMA threshold from FIFO
 depth

The T8010 DMA eligibility check uses a literal transfer length of 17
bytes. That value is the first length which exceeds the controller's
16-entry FIFO, but the relationship is not visible at the call site and is
easy to misinterpret as a peripheral requirement.

Define the threshold as one entry beyond APPLE_SPI_FIFO_DEPTH and use that
name in the controller's DMA predicate. The existing word-alignment,
TX-buffer and half-duplex restrictions remain unchanged, so error handling
and PIO fallback behavior are unaffected.

This remains a controller-local capability decision; neither SPI core
policy nor a device-specific property is needed. The complete iPhone 7
touch series was built with Image.gz, DTBs and modules, and the T8010 SPI
path was exercised by the D111 touchscreen hardware test. This patch was
also checked with checkpatch.pl --strict.

Signed-off-by: Paul Praschl <praschlpaul@g-p.at>

Orchard-replay-of: f131d2c49bfd09a8331fbc681b459cd9b020c306
---
 drivers/spi/spi-apple.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/spi/spi-apple.c b/drivers/spi/spi-apple.c
index 7d0c812ee..1a2e43beb 100644
--- a/drivers/spi/spi-apple.c
+++ b/drivers/spi/spi-apple.c
@@ -101,6 +101,7 @@
 #define APPLE_SPI_DELAY_POST		0x168
 
 #define APPLE_SPI_FIFO_DEPTH		16
+#define APPLE_SPI_T8010_DMA_MIN_LEN	(APPLE_SPI_FIFO_DEPTH + 1)
 
 /*
  * The slowest refclock available is 24MHz, the highest divider is 0x7ff,
@@ -396,7 +397,8 @@ static bool apple_spi_t8010_can_dma(struct spi_controller *ctlr,
 		bits_per_word = 8;
 
 	return ctlr->dma_tx && (bits_per_word == 8 || bits_per_word == 16) &&
-	       t->len >= 17 && !(t->len % (bits_per_word / 8)) &&
+	       t->len >= APPLE_SPI_T8010_DMA_MIN_LEN &&
+	       !(t->len % (bits_per_word / 8)) &&
 	       t->tx_buf && !t->rx_buf;
 }
 
